{"index":0,"content":"\n\n<think>\nThe user wants a C++20 function that:\n1. Validates balanced brackets (round, square, curly)\n2. Ignores brackets inside quoted strings (both single and double quotes)\n3. Includes a compact self-test\n4. Returns code only\n\nLet me think about the design:\n\n- I need to track whether I'm inside a string (single or double quoted)\n- Handle escape characters (backslash) inside strings\n- Use a stack for bracket matching\n- Brackets to check: (), [], {}\n\nEdge cases:\n- Escaped quotes inside strings: \"she said \\\"hi\\\"\"\n- Escaped backslashes: \"path\\\\to\\\\file\"\n- Single quotes: 'hello'\n- Nested brackets\n- Unbalanced brackets\n- Brackets inside strings should be ignored\n\nLet me write this:\n\n```cpp\n#include <string>\n#include <stack>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <iostream>\n\nbool balanced(const std::string& s) {\n    std::stack<char> st;\n    char quote = 0;\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < s.size(); ++i) {\n        char c = s[i];\n        if (quote) {\n            if (c == '\\\\' && i + 1 < s.size()) { ++i; continue; }\n            if (c == quote) quote = 0;\n        } else {\n            if (c == '\"' || c == '\\'') { quote = c; continue; }\n            if (c == '(' || c == '[' || c == '{') st.push(c);\n            else if (c == ')' || c == ']' || c == '}') {\n                if (st.empty()) return false;\n                char top = st.top(); st.pop();\n                if ((c == ')' && top != '(') ||\n                    (c == ']' && top != '[') ||\n                    (c == '}' && top != '{')) return false;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return st.empty() && !quote;\n}\n```\n\nWait, should I also consider that an unclosed string makes it invalid? I'll say yes - if we're still in a quote at the end, it's unbalanced/invalid.\n\nNow for the self-test, I'll use a compact approach with a helper macro or just a series of asserts in main","tokens":[],"id_slot":0,"stop":true,"model":"qwen3.8-27b@q4_k_m","tokens_predicted":512,"tokens_evaluated":28,"generation_settings":{"seed":202,"temperature":0.6000000238418579,"dynatemp_range":0.0,"dynatemp_exponent":1.0,"top_k":20,"top_p":0.949999988079071,"min_p":0.0,"top_n_sigma":-1.0,"xtc_probability":0.0,"xtc_threshold":0.10000000149011612,"typical_p":1.0,"repeat_last_n":64,"repeat_penalty":1.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"dry_multiplier":0.0,"dry_base":1.75,"dry_allowed_length":2,"dry_penalty_last_n":64,"dry_sequence_breakers":["\n",":","\"","*"],"mirostat":0,"mirostat_tau":5.0,"mirostat_eta":0.10000000149011612,"adaptive_target":-1.0,"adaptive_decay":0.8999999761581421,"stop":[],"max_tokens":512,"n_predict":512,"n_keep":0,"n_discard":0,"ignore_eos":false,"stream":false,"logit_bias":[],"n_probs":0,"min_keep":0,"grammar":"","grammar_lazy":false,"grammar_triggers":[],"preserved_tokens":[],"chat_format":"Content-only","reasoning_format":"auto","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":false,"lora":[]},"prompt":"Write a C++20 function that validates balanced brackets while ignoring brackets inside quoted strings. Include a compact self-test. Return code only.","has_new_line":true,"truncated":false,"stop_type":"limit","stopping_word":"","tokens_cached":539,"timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":28,"prompt_ms":137.119,"prompt_per_token_ms":4.897107142857143,"prompt_per_second":204.20218933918713,"predicted_n":512,"predicted_ms":13258.267,"predicted_per_token_ms":25.945727984344423,"predicted_per_second":38.541990442642316}}